{50}{Every man has his secrets.  Believe me, I understand...}{}{5}{}{74}{re +5}
{51}{Perhaps you could better acquaint me with the criminal mind...}{}{5}{}{57}{re -10}
{52}{I've no doubt you've plenty to hide, sir...}{}{5}{}{67}{re -5}
{54}{Uh...okay.  I ask you more questions...?}{}{-4}{}{26}{}
{55}{E:}{}{1}{}{0}{}
{57}{[He takes a step closer, looming over you.]  What?  Are you intimating that I'm a criminal?  You know nothing of me, friend.  I suggest you reconsider your words...I'm not a man to be insulted...}{[He takes a step closer, looming over you.]  What?  Are you intimating that I'm a criminal?  You know nothing of me, friend.  I suggest you reconsider your words...I'm not a man to be insulted...}{}{}{}{}
{58}{I've no wish for trouble.  If you're no criminal, then what are you?}{}{5}{}{62}{}
{59}{I've dealt with criminal rubbish like you before.  Step away.}{}{5}{}{}{co, fl 21}
{60}{E:}{}{5}{}{0}{}
{62}{I told you...I've no wish to speak of it.  Especially not with the denizens of this god-forsaken Isle.  There's not a man among you would understand the things I've endured...}{I told you...I've no wish to speak of it.  Especially not with the denizens of this god-forsaken Isle.  There's not a man among you would understand the things I've endured...}{}{}{}{}
{63}{I'm sure you're right.  I've weathered much already myself...}{}{5}{}{67}{}
{64}{Your wallowing sickens me, old man...}{}{5}{}{}{co, fl 21}
{65}{E:}{}{5}{}{0}{}
{67}{[He smirks at you.]  No offense, young man, but you haven't the slightest idea as to what my life is here, or what it was before.  No doubt you were shipped here due to some reproachable offense...thievery, murder.  You're all the same...}{[He smirks at you.]  No offense, young lady, but you haven't the slightest idea as to what my life is here, or what it was before.  No doubt you were shipped here due to some reproachable offense...thievery, murder.  You're all the same...}{}{}{}{}
{68}{Actually, I came here of my own accord...}{}{5}{}{187}{}
{69}{You're making unwarranted assumptions.  A young man's mistake...}{}{5}{ch 15}{74}{re +5}
{70}{You're making unwarranted assumptions.  A young man's mistake...}{}{5}{ch -14}{79}{re -5}
{71}{Old man are the same as well...senile and weak...}{}{5}{}{}{co, fl 21}
{72}{E:}{}{5}{}{0}{}
{74}{[He seems a little surprised.  He gives you a shrewd look, making a new appraisal.]  You're right.  Please, forgive my short-sightedness.  No doubt you've things of value to share as well.  Perhaps you and I might have something to speak of after all...}{[He seems a little surprised.  He gives you a shrewd look, making a new appraisal.]  You're right.  Please, forgive my short-sightedness.  No doubt you've things of value to share as well.  Perhaps you and I might have something to speak of after all...}{}{}{}{}
{75}{I'd enjoy that.  Tell me of yourself, Maximillian...}{}{5}{}{89}{}
{76}{I doubt it.  I don't confide in degenerates like yourself...}{}{5}{}{}{co, fl 21}
{77}{Perhaps later.  I'll return in a while...}{}{5}{}{0}{lf1 1}
{79}{[Your comment does little but annoy him.]  And who are you to judge me?  You've not the years to warrant such an opinion, boy.  Perhaps it's best that you leave...}{[Your comment does little but annoy him.]  And who are you to judge me?  You've not the years to warrant such an opinion, girl.  Perhaps it's best that you leave...}{}{}{}{}
{80}{Wisdom is not only weighed in years, but also in words...}{}{5}{}{74}{re +10}
{81}{Aged wine is smooth, but older wine is sour...}{}{5}{}{}{re -5, fl 85}
{82}{I tire of your words, old man.  I'm going to put an end to them...}{}{5}{}{}{co, fl 21}
{83}{E:}{}{5}{}{0}{}
{85}{This conversation is over, friend.  You'd best leave, and now.  I won't warn you again...}{This conversation is over, friend.  You'd best leave, and now.  I won't warn you again...}{}{}{}{}
{89}{Perhaps now is a good time to tell stories.  But forgive me if I'm a little leery of companionship.  I've spent many years out here in the wilds by myself.  Might I ask you to tell me of yourself before I begin?}{Perhaps now is a good time to tell stories.  But forgive me if I'm a little leery of companionship.  I've spent many years out here in the wilds by myself.  Might I ask you to tell me of yourself before I begin?}{}{}{}{}
{90}{I'd rather not speak of my past, nor of my reasons for being here...}{}{5}{}{}{lf2 1, re -5, fl 94}
{91}{Of course.  It began not long ago...[Tell him your tale.]}{}{5}{}{96}{re +5}
{92}{Perhaps another time.  I'll return later.}{}{5}{}{0}{lf1 1, lc1 1, fl 93}
{93}{Yes...I'd be interested in speaking with you again...please return...}{Yes...I'd be interested in speaking with you again...please return...}{}{}{}{}
{94}{That's a shame.  Perhaps I misjudged you, friend.  Maybe it's better we don't speak after all.  I bid you good day...}{That's a shame.  Perhaps I misjudged you, friend.  Maybe it's better we don't speak after all.  I bid you good day...}{}{}{}{}
{95}{I think we've spoken enough, friend.  Leave me be...}{I think we've spoken enough, friend.  Leave me be...}{}{}{}{}
{96}{[He is silent for a long time.  Then...]  It seems grave times have come to Arcanum.  And somehow you've become entangled in her problems.  You're a brave soul, sir.  Few are those who would do the things you've done...}{[He is silent for a long time.  Then...]  It seems grave times have come to Arcanum.  And somehow you've become entangled in her problems.  You're a brave soul, madam.  Few are those who would do the things you've done...}{}{}{}{}
{97}{I just want people to stop trying to kill me...}{}{5}{}{101}{}
{98}{Virtue and valor allow me to act in no other way...}{}{5}{}{104}{re +5}
{99}{My reasons are my own.  Make no judgments concerning them...}{}{5}{}{101}{re -5}
{101}{We've all our reasons, I suppose.  I'm not a man to judge one way or another.  But I do know that, in the end, a man is the sum of his actions.  You will be weighed in the same manner...}{We've all our reasons, I suppose.  I'm not a man to judge one way or another.  But I do know that, in the end, a person is the sum of his or her actions.  You will be weighed in the same manner...}{}{}{}{}
{102}{Why don't you tell me your story, Maximillian...?}{}{5}{}{107}{}
{104}{[Maximillian smiles.]  You've no idea how refreshing it is to hear someone speak in such a noble manner, sir.  There were years I believed that there were no men left in this land who knew what those words meant...}{[Maximillian smiles.]  You've no idea how refreshing it is to hear someone speak in such a noble manner, madam.  There were years I believed that there were no men left in this land who knew what those words meant...}{}{}{}{}
{105}{Why don't you tell me your story, Maximillian...?}{}{5}{}{107}{}
{107}{Yes...it is long past time that someone know my tale.  Tell me friend...do you know of anything of the kingdom of Cumbria?  Her capital city of Dernholm?  King Praetor the First?}{Yes...it is long past time that someone know my tale.  Tell me friend...do you know of anything of the kingdom of Cumbria?  Her capital city of Dernholm?  King Praetor the First?}{}{}{}{}
{108}{I've heard things about that place, but I know very little...}{}{5}{}{112}{}
{109}{I've been there before...}{}{5}{}{112}{}
{110}{I know nothing of Cumbria...}{}{5}{}{112}{}
{112}{I see.  The Cumbria I speak of was a much different place...far different than what it is today, I'm sure.  I speak of a time when Cumbria was a powerful kingdom, when the elves and dwarves would come to her walls to pay tribute to her king.  When the banners of the famed Dragon Knights were a thing to be respected and feared...}{I see.  The Cumbria I speak of was a much different place...far different than what it is today, I'm sure.  I speak of a time when Cumbria was a powerful kingdom, when the elves and dwarves would come to her walls to pay tribute to her king.  When the banners of the famed Dragon Knights were a thing to be respected and feared...}{}{}{}{}
{113}{I take it Cumbria is no longer that place?}{}{5}{}{116}{}
{114}{I've seen Cumbria...it falls far from what you describe...}{}{5}{}{116}{}
{116}{No...there's no doubt that Cumbria is but a shadow of her former glory.  The day came long ago when her fate was sealed.  The day when technology began to rival magic, when the old ways began to fall to the new...}{No...there's no doubt that Cumbria is but a shadow of her former glory.  The day came long ago when her fate was sealed.  The day when technology began to rival magic, when the old ways began to fall to the new...}{}{}{}{}
{117}{What happened?  Did Cumbria resist that change?}{}{5}{}{120}{}
{118}{Let us speak of this later...}{}{5}{}{}{lc1 2, fl 178}
{120}{Yes, and vehemently.  My...the King at the time, Torren, was a wise and brave man, but set in his ways. [Maximillian smiles, sadly.]  He was cut from sterner stuff, but he was like stone...unwavering, but inflexible.  He failed to see how Cumbria needed to grow, to change...}{Yes, and vehemently.  My...the King at the time, Torren, was a wise and brave man, but set in his ways. [Maximillian smiles, sadly.]  He was cut from sterner stuff, but he was like stone...unwavering, but inflexible.  He failed to see how Cumbria needed to grow, to change...}{}{}{}{}
{121}{And so?}{}{5}{}{123}{}
{123}{And so, he passed laws outlawing the use of technology in his lands, and set a ruling council of mage advisors at his side.  For years Cumbria was still very strong and influential, but it was only a matter of time...}{And so, he passed laws outlawing the use of technology in his lands, and set a ruling council of mage advisors at his side.  For years Cumbria was still very strong and influential, but it was only a matter of time...}{}{}{}{}
{124}{What happened?}{}{5}{}{127}{}
{125}{Let us speak of this later...}{}{5}{}{}{lc1 3, fl 178}
{127}{Well, Cumbria was surpassed, both in commerce and in power.  When mighty Tarant demanded the release of certain disputed lands, Cumbria was taught a harsh lesson.  The armies of Cumbria were slaughtered, the Dragon Knights cut down by gun and cannonfire.  The glory of older days was lost...}{Well, Cumbria was surpassed, both in commerce and in power.  When mighty Tarant demanded the release of certain disputed lands, Cumbria was taught a harsh lesson.  The armies of Cumbria were slaughtered, the Dragon Knights cut down by gun and cannonfire.  The glory of older days was lost...}{}{}{}{}
{128}{And what of King Torren?  What happened to him...}{}{5}{}{131}{}
{131}{[Maximillian looks to the horizon; he is far away.]  He was killed.  He led the final charge of the Dragon Knights, and was shot as any common soldier.  Unwavering and brave to the end...}{[Maximillian looks to the horizon; he is far away.]  He was killed.  He led the final charge of the Dragon Knights, and was shot as any common soldier.  Unwavering and brave to the end...}{}{}{}{}
{132}{I see.  What does all of this have to do with you, Maximillian...?}{}{5}{}{135}{}
{133}{Let us speak of this later...}{}{5}{}{}{lc1 4, fl 178}
{135}{[He seems to come to himself, looking back at you.]  With the death of Torren came a power struggle. There were those who believed that Cumbria should embrace the new age, to seek a better way and make her powerful again...}{[He seems to come to himself, looking back at you.]  With the death of Torren came a power struggle. There were those who believed that Cumbria should embrace the new age, to seek a better way and make her powerful again...}{}{}{}{}
{136}{But others thought differently...?}{}{5}{}{138}{}
{138}{Yes.  Some people cannot see the answer, even when it is laid before them in the form of a dead King.  Torren had two sons...the older son believed in the new ways, and the younger son believed in nothing.  And so, the mage council that Torren had put in place put their influence behind the younger son...}{Yes.  Some people cannot see the answer, even when it is laid before them in the form of a dead King.  Torren had two sons...the older son believed in the new ways, and the younger son believed in nothing.  And so, the mage council that Torren had put in place put their influence behind the younger son...}{}{}{}{}
{139}{Wasn't the older son heir to the throne by birthright?}{}{5}{}{146}{}
{140}{Wait...I'm a little unclear as to all of this...}{}{5}{}{143}{}
{141}{Let us speak of this later...}{}{5}{}{}{lc1 5, fl 178}
{143}{Cumbria was a powerful kingdom before the advent of technology.  King Torren resisted the changes that were happening in the world and outlawed the use of technology.  He died in a battle with Tarant, and there was a struggle for the throne between his two sons.}{Cumbria was a powerful kingdom before the advent of technology.  King Torren resisted the changes that were happening in the world and outlawed the use of technology.  He died in a battle with Tarant, and there was a struggle for the throne between his two sons.}{}{}{}{}
{144}{Thank you.  But wasn't the older son heir to the throne?}{}{5}{}{146}{}
{146}{Yes, but men will create all manner of evil in pursuit of power.  The mage council, who controlled the younger son, brought false allegations against the older son, charging him with treason.  He was taken in the night, and sent away to rot in prison for the rest of his days...}{Yes, but men will create all manner of evil in pursuit of power.  The mage council, who controlled the younger son, brought false allegations against the older son, charging him with treason.  He was taken in the night, and sent away to rot in prison for the rest of his days...}{}{}{}{}
{147}{The older son...by the gods...!}{}{5}{}{149}{}
{149}{Yes, stranger.  The older son was me.  I was sent here by my own brother, King Praetor the First of Cumbria.  And I've been here ever since...}{Yes, stranger.  The older son was me.  I was sent here by my own brother, King Praetor the First of Cumbria.  And I've been here ever since...}{}{}{}{}
{150}{I don't know what to say.  I've no words...}{}{5}{}{154}{re +5}
{151}{Such are the vagaries of politics, Maximillian}{}{5}{}{158}{re -5}
{152}{That's a shame, old boy.  Well...I must be going...}{}{5}{}{161}{re -5}
{154}{No words are necessary, friend.  You've done enough to sit here and listen to my story.  I've made peace with my past...life here on the Isle is harsh, but a man learns to live with himself, to accept what life brings. }{No words are necessary, friend.  You've done enough to sit here and listen to my story.  I've made peace with my past...life here on the Isle is harsh, but a man learns to live with himself, to accept what life brings. }{}{}{}{}
{155}{But it was so unfair.  Perhaps I could bring you home...}{}{5}{}{164}{}
{156}{I see.  I must be going, Maximillian...}{}{5}{}{161}{}
{158}{That seems a fairly shallow assessment of my situation, friend.  I've no longer any interest in speaking about this...}{That seems a fairly shallow assessment of my situation, friend.  I've no longer any interest in speaking about this...}{}{}{}{}
{159}{Neither do I.  Good day to you.}{}{5}{}{}{lf2 1, fl 94}
{160}{Wait...forgive the offense.  Perhaps I could bring you home...}{}{5}{}{164}{}
{161}{[He seems a little disappointed, but not overly so.]  I see.  Well, I'm glad you were here to listen to my story.  I can rest well knowing that my memory will not die with me.  Thank you, friend...}{[He seems a little disappointed, but not overly so.]  I see.  Well, I'm glad you were here to listen to my story.  I can rest well knowing that my memory will not die with me.  Thank you, friend...}{}{}{}{}
{162}{Good day to you, Maximillian...}{}{5}{}{0}{lf4 1}
{164}{No.  My time in Cumbria has passed.  If my brother lives, I'm sure he has paid the price due him.  He was young and foolish...when one is a King, life is unforgiving when you live so...}{No.  My time in Cumbria has passed.  If my brother lives, I'm sure he has paid the price due him.  He was young and foolish...when one is a King, life is unforgiving when you live so...}{}{}{}{}
{165}{But Cumbria...perhaps the kingdom still needs you...}{}{5}{}{167}{}
{167}{[He looks at you, then away to the west.]  I can still feel her, you know...the stone walls of Dernholm, the rolling hills and vales, the trumpet blast of the Dragon Knights marching to battle.  I wake up sometimes, and I forget where I am...}{[He looks at you, then away to the west.]  I can still feel her, you know...the stone walls of Dernholm, the rolling hills and vales, the trumpet blast of the Dragon Knights marching to battle.  I wake up sometimes, and I forget where I am...}{}{}{}{}
{168}{Come back with me, Maximillian.  It's not too late...}{}{5}{}{170}{}
{170}{[He looks back again.]  Perhaps.  I will ask you this, friend.  The Captain of the Dragon Knights was a man named Warren Pel Dar.  He was my one true friend.  If he still lives, and cares to do so, tell him I am here, and that I'd enjoy once more the pleasure of his company...}{[He looks back again.]  Perhaps.  I will ask you this, friend.  The Captain of the Dragon Knights was a man named Warren Pel Dar.  He was my one true friend.  If he still lives, and cares to do so, tell him I am here, and that I'd enjoy once more the pleasure of his company...}{}{}{}{}
